  "caption": "Quinn lost three rounds to a jam jar, then noticed creaky fingers and little bumps on the joints. Was it all that knitting?\n\nHand arthritis is common, especially after 50, and it's mostly down to genes and age rather than hobbies. The joints may change shape, but pain often settles and hands can stay useful.\n\nThings that often help: warm water in the morning, gentle finger movement plus graded grip and pinch work, handy gadgets like jar openers and thicker pens, and keeping your hands in everyday use.\n\nIf knuckles and wrists swell on both sides, stiffness lasts over an hour, or you feel unwell, see your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
